## File 2 — CreateTaskComponent.tsx (blank-submit validation, 4 hunks) — reused the EXACT taskName/taskUrl/siteType required-field pattern
1. Ref (:579), beside the other field refs:
   `const descriptionFieldRef = React.useRef<HTMLDivElement>(null);`
2. Validity + error string (:598-601), beside taskNameError/taskUrlError:
```
const isDescriptionValid = Array.isArray(save.Description) && save.Description.some((b: any) =>
    (b?.Title?.trim?.() ?? '') !== '' ||
    (Array.isArray(b?.Subtext) && b.Subtext.some((s: any) => (s?.Title?.trim?.() ?? '') !== '')));
const descriptionError = !isDescriptionValid ? 'Please enter a description.' : '';
```
3. Show-gate (:605), beside showTaskNameError etc.:
   `const showDescriptionError = submitAttempted && !!descriptionError;`
   (Gated on submitAttempted only — the description editor has no fieldTouched key/onBlur to hook; submitAttempted is the same trigger the other three fields use to force-show on submit. Error therefore does NOT show on load, only after a blank submit attempt.)
4. Guard inside validateFormForSubmit (:645-648), appended after the isSiteValid guard, before `return true`:
```
if (!isDescriptionValid) {
    scrollToField(descriptionFieldRef);
    return false;
}
```
5. Render (:3189, :3197-3199): added `ref={descriptionFieldRef}` to the Description `<div className="mt-3">` and, after <CreateTaskDescription/>, the error span mirroring the taskUrl one:
```
{showDescriptionError ? (
    <span className="mt-1 block text-xs text-red-600">{descriptionError}</span>
) : null}
```
createTask() already gates on `if (!validateFormForSubmit()) { ...; return; }` (:1811-1815), so returning false blocks submit — nothing is serialized, so no empty description box reaches the FeedBackDescriptions mapping at :2146.

## Which existing validation pattern I reused
The taskName / taskUrl / siteType required-field idiom: isXValid + xError string (:585-601) -> showXError gate (:597-605) -> `if (!isXValid){ scrollToField(ref); return false; }` in validateFormForSubmit (:625-648) -> red `text-xs text-red-600` span + field ref in render. Same error surface, same styling, same gating point. No new toast/alert/framework introduced. NOTE: the DirectTask/burger branch of validateFormForSubmit (:611-615) returns early and is NOT description-gated — this matches how it already bypasses taskUrl/site validation for that flow; I left it as-is (in scope only the standard Create Task submit).

## Verification — what I actually ran
- esbuild.transform (Vite's own transformer, loader tsx, jsx automatic) on BOTH changed files: `OK transform` for each — no JSX/TS syntax errors. This is the cheap reliable gate; I did NOT run `npm run typecheck` (known-unreliable here per your note: @types/d3-dispatch .d.ts masks app errors) and did NOT run full build.
- grep confirmed all 5 insertion sites present at the lines above and the child effect at :75-79.
- Logic trace of acceptance criteria: (load) seed emits 1 empty box, showDescriptionError=false (submitAttempted false) -> one open box, no error, no click needed. (blank submit) submitAttempted=true, isDescriptionValid=false -> validateFormForSubmit returns false, scrolls to description, red 'Please enter a description.' shows, createTask returns before serialize -> nothing saved. (with text) isDescriptionValid=true -> submit proceeds, box persists via existing :2146 mapping.
- NOT run by me (needs the live browser — Handoff/human step): the interactive dev-render steps (`npm run dev`, click-through of load/type/add-remove, actual blank vs filled submit, task opening in the popup). I did not drive the browser, so I make no claim those passed — please route to Handoff for the human live-render confirmation.

## Residual risk
Low. Mechanical, idiom-matched, confined to the two fenced files. One thing for the human render to confirm: that requiring a non-empty description does not block any legitimate existing flow that intentionally creates a task with no description (I found no such required exception in the standard submit path; DirectTask/burger flow is unaffected as noted)."
}

